  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Add a guide under `docs/user-guide/` for one external MCP agent connected to both desktop apps.\n- Give a Claude Code configuration with explicit stdio bridges and separate loopback ports.\n- Walk through a plate with one hole: create, save, import, inspect the link, detect, generate and verify.\n- Document the native `.sc` cache restrictions and the STEP fallback.\n- Explain separate undo histories, manual post and machine approval, and external-agent cloud privacy.\n- Link the guide from the README. Record the scope decision in a separate decision file.\n\nThis documents the external-agent path from #3793. It does not implement the proposed in-app MCP client or privacy policy.\n\n## Sources\n\n- CamCraft source at `034e91b8b78fa64989d18e1d5d17344531c4762c`: the live tool registry and schemas, import path, model-link tool, window watcher, native cache reader and live approval gate.\n- Public SolidCraft MCP documentation and modeling reference at `69ac4646de58dc64befd804157e95120a1622803`. The guide links these exact revisions.\n- Existing `camcraft-cli mcp --help`, `mcp reference`, and a read-only MCP `initialize` / `tools/list` exchange.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused documentation audit: pass. The audit parses 21 JSON table calls, checks CamCraft names and required/top-level arguments and types against the CLI schemas, and compares the CLI's 124 tool names with the current source registry.\n- Relative links: all 9 guide links resolve. The README link resolves. The client configuration parses as JSON.\n- Both connection commands agree with current CamCraft source/help and public SolidCraft documentation.\n- The baseline presence check fails because the requested page is absent on the base. The new page passes the focused checks. This is not a runtime regression test.\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run`: zero steps. This is a selection result, not a passing test run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- SolidCraft was not installed or run. The complete two-app walkthrough was not run.\n- No GUI check, posting, machine execution or physical safety test was performed.\n- No Rust application build, Rust test suite, Clippy, example catalog, heavy or release gate was run for this prose-only change.\n- The repository's review-time light lane was not run. This scoped documentation change uses the focused source, schema and link checks above.\n- The deployed documentation site was not built or changed.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: low. No escalation.\n\nFixes #3815\n",
